^["risk_model"]{
 hard_failures: [
  "the move leaves refs from outside the cut pointing at the dated path",
  "the snapshot tag names a commit whose cut differs from the shelved one",
  "a mechanical pass rewrites a claim statement or renames an anchor"
 ]
 soft_failures: [
  "LSP and graph caches keep the old path until reindexed",
  "open worktrees and plan streams still name the dated path"
 ]
 recoveries: [
  "spw resolve and the cut gate run after every commit; any unresolved ref blocks the commit",
  "plan streams are history and keep the old path; cards and roots follow the move"
 ]
 non_negotiables: [
  "no anchor is renamed or reused; the permanence rule holds",
  "claim statements stay byte-identical through mechanical passes",
  "the raw shelf and its quarantine stay untouched",
  "commits and the snapshot tag are authorized by the owner"
 ]
}

^["validation"]{
 hypotheses: [
  "H1 the move changes no anchor and no ref target: 8180 anchors before and after, and the only unresolved refs that change are the three panel refs this plan fixes",
  "H2 the receipt ledger loses nothing: every file, event, at, agent, care, and outcome tuple is recoverable from journal entries",
  "H3 receipts to the journal and a trimmed card cut at least 15 percent of lines with claim statements byte-identical",
  "H4 an agent given only the extension door and the gate adds one surface that passes the gate",
  "H5 anchor-addressed refs remove about 400 thousand characters, about 8 percent of the cut"
 ]
 negative_controls: [
  "git diff of the raw shelf directories is empty",
  "the quarantine list in .spw/caches/index.spw is unchanged",
  "the sorted list of claim statement strings is identical before and after each mechanical pass"
 ]
 demo_path: [
  "open .spw/caches/cut/index.spw and follow the extension door",
  "add one surface in a worktree and run the gate",
  "check out the tag caches-cut/2026.09.30 and find the dated cut as it was shelved"
 ]
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] observe — The cut holds 439 files and 86604 lines; 68 percent of its characters sit inside strings. Path refs are 663 thousand characters, about 417 thousand of them path prefix, though anchors are already unique across the cut. The emit and provenance blocks are 14724 lines, receipts 2717 lines. 322 of about 600 concept tags occur once. The cut has no root index; the gate fails on three refs to panels nobody has written; the caches index still routes only to the raw shelf.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] decide — The owner chose samples first, then parser changes, for the syntax revision, staged under syntax-hardware-alignment, whose rule is samples before any parser change.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] decide — The owner chose a living tree with git-tag snapshots over extending the dated directory in place or opening a new dated cut per pass.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] decide — The owner asked for a directory for dated .spw files, a journal. It opens at .spw/journal at the canon root, entries named YYYY-MM-DD-slug.spw; resume notes, snapshot manifests, and receipt ledgers are its first kinds of entry.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] decide — The living tree is .spw/caches/cut; the raw shelf stays where it is, per the owner decision recorded in the caches-cut-2026-09-30 plan.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] taste — The contract is 232 lines and every rule in it is real, but an extending agent needs a door of about forty lines: where to put a surface, which exemplar to copy, which namespace to write under, which gate to run, and where its receipt goes.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[anchor_ref_form]: "Which form addresses an anchor without its path: a cut-scoped fragment ~\"#src_creator_epub33\", a root figure with a fragment such as @cut#src_creator_epub33, or a new anchor-ref mark? The samples show all three; the owner picks before any parser change."
 ?[snapshot_tag]: "Is caches-cut/2026.09.30 on main at 813444dc the right tag? Its cut matches dfed5cc6 except one line in spw/history/editor-extension-arcs.spw."
 ?[season_home]: "Do season/ and trails/season-2026-q4.spw stay in the living tree with as_of, or move to the journal as dated entries?"
}

^["commits"]{
 ~[plan]: ".[plans] — caches-living-tree plans the living cut, the journal, and leaner cache syntax"
 ~[journal_open]: "#[journal] — .spw/journal holds dated surfaces, routed from the canon index; the caches resume note is its first entry"
 ~[cut_snapshot]: ".[journal] — the shelved cut is tagged caches-cut/2026.09.30 and its manifest is a journal entry"
 ~[cut_move]: "&[caches] — the cut lives at .spw/caches/cut, undated; the gate, the caches index, docs, and plan roots follow"
 ~[cut_door]: ".[caches] — the cut gets a root index with relevance tiers and an extension door, and the gate passes"
 ~[syntax_samples]: "^seed[caches] — samples for anchor-addressed refs, journal receipts, a lean card, and closed concepts, as proposals p8 to p11"
 ~[authorship_pilot]: ".[caches] — making/authorship rewritten with the sampled forms that parse today"
 ~[concept_vocab]: "#[caches] — concepts become a closed vocabulary and the gate enforces it"
 ~[receipts_to_journal]: "&[caches] — per-surface receipts move to journal ledgers; each surface keeps as_of and one line that names its ledger"
 ~[card_trim]: "&[caches] — cards drop fields the title comment and the sources already carry"
 ~[anchor_refs]: "^seed[resolver] — conditional on ?[anchor_ref_form]: anchor-addressed refs resolve in the CLI, the LSP, and the gate"
 ~[anchor_refs_migrate]: "&[caches] — conditional on ~[anchor_refs]: refs into the cut drop their path prefix"
}

